## Deutsche Bahn Case Study

Deutsche Bahn (DB) operates one of Europe's largest railway networks.

Every day,

thousands of trains travel across Germany.

The railway system must continuously optimize

- train routes,
- maintenance schedules,
- resource allocation,
- disruption recovery.

Many of these problems resemble the Travelling Salesman Problem or Vehicle Routing Problem.

Quantum Annealing offers an attractive approach because these scheduling problems can often be formulated as QUBO optimization problems.

Although classical optimization remains dominant today,

hybrid quantum-classical methods are expected to become increasingly important as quantum hardware continues to improve.

