# 7.12 Current Industrial Challenges

Despite growing interest,

industrial adoption remains limited by several factors.

These include

- Immature hardware
- Limited quantum expertise
- High implementation costs
- Integration with existing IT systems
- Difficulty identifying suitable optimization problems
- Lack of proven quantum advantage in every application

As quantum hardware matures,

many of these barriers are expected to decrease.

